title: $SESSION_ID is not a variable, so a cloud claim silently records a pid
created: 2026-09-18T17:33:09Z
updated: 2026-09-18T17:33:09Z
effort: S
area: cli
handoff:

Both generated documents tell an agent with no checkable process to claim
like this:

  AGENTS.md:46          PIDLY_AGENT=$SESSION_ID PIDLY_LEASE=2h pidly claim 7
  .pidly/README.md:273  the same line

SESSION_ID is not set by anything. Under Claude Code the variable is
CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID; plain SESSION_ID is unset, so the line expands to
PIDLY_AGENT= and the agent has no way to notice.

holder() tests [ -n "${PIDLY_AGENT:-}" ], so an empty value is not an error.
It falls through to the pid branch and the claim records this machine's pid
for a session that may be on no machine here:

  PIDLY_AGENT=$SESSION_ID PIDLY_LEASE=2h pidly claim 1
  1 claimed by 751.130120276@31917916.u1000 2026-09-17T...

Wrong rather than fatal — the lease still frees it, and claim_state calls
another runtime's pid unverifiable rather than dead, so nothing is stolen.
What is lost is the thing the agent branch exists for: a name a human can
read, and a claim that cannot be confused with a local process.

Two decisions, and they are separable:

- What the documents should say. Naming CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID in the
  format's own reference makes it a Claude document, which the format has
  refused everywhere else — AGENTS.md is written for four assistants and
  pidly claude exists precisely so the Claude-specific parts live in a file
  of their own. A placeholder the reader must replace, like
  PIDLY_AGENT=ci-run-4821, says what the field is for and cannot be
  copy-pasted into a silent fallback.
- Whether an empty PIDLY_AGENT should die. Set-but-empty is almost always a
  variable that did not exist, not a caller asking for pid identity: the
  caller who wants a pid does not set the variable at all. Dying on it turns
  this whole class of mistake loud at the point it happens. Against: it is a
  behaviour change, and a wrapper that exports PIDLY_AGENT="" unconditionally
  would start failing.

Found while answering 33, which is where the evidence is written down.

Done when the published line cannot mislead an agent that runs it verbatim,
the empty-value decision is made and written down, and the suite covers
whichever behaviour is chosen.
